WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:02.420
It's the season of giving.

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:05.830
For Kazi Mannan, this means going into overdrive.

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:10.570
Kazi is an immigrant from Pakistan, who now
owns a small but successful restaurant in

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.769
downtown Washington DC.

00:00:12.769 --> 00:00:18.750
All of these scarves and warm clothes that
he purchased are about to be given away.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:24.000
This is an annual gathering at Franklin Square
park, in downtown DC, where various charities

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.990
and churches will give away food and goods
to people in need just before Christmas.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:32.730
Kazi has been coming for the past four years,
ever since he opened his restaurant, and has

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.570
built up a small network of homeless people
who know him.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:54.450
"It's a joy, anything that you can make another
person happy...if you can put a smile on someone

00:00:54.450 --> 00:01:03.170
else's face, it's a big blessing."

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:06.640
Kazi said he also knows the sting of being
poor.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:14.170
The restaurant he now owns, serves free meals
to homeless people all day, every day.

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:17.990
"Homelessness is endemic in Washington DC.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:23.000
One estimate said 11,000 people have to sleep
on the streets every night.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.590
Kazi Mannan himself said that he has experienced
a similar situation of extreme poverty.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:33.630
And now that he's a successful business owner,
he wants to give back."

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:37.990
Sakina Grill now has a many regular non-paying
customers.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:43.119
Besides the benefit of freshly made food,
one man told us, it helps him simply feel

00:01:43.119 --> 00:01:44.150
accepted.

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:55.810
"It makes you feel regular, like normal...it
kind of makes you feel privileged too."

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:03.970
Kazi's generosity started when the restaurant
started on day one.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:08.899
Seeing homeless people digging through trash
cans broke his heart, he said.

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:21.450
"I promised that if I ever had a restaurant,
I would have this philosophy...it

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:38.659
will benefit me, and will benefit others."

00:02:38.659 --> 00:02:43.799
Over the past four years, Sakina Grill is
still operational, and has given out more

00:02:43.799 --> 00:02:45.939
than 80,000 meals.

00:02:45.939 --> 00:02:48.639
A good reminder that need knows no season.

